# Intentionally present, and intentionally empty of rules.
#
# When a package has no .npmignore, npm falls back to .gitignore when deciding what to pack. The
# published assets/ directory is generated at build time and therefore git-ignored, so that
# fallback would ship a package with no rules file and no dictionaries — a tool that installs
# cleanly and then crashes on its first command.
#
# Current npm versions let the "files" allowlist in package.json win over .gitignore, so this
# file changes nothing today. It stays because that precedence has moved between npm versions
# before, and the failure it prevents is silent and only visible after publishing.
#
# Source maps are NOT excluded here: "files" also wins over .npmignore, so they are deleted by
# scripts/prepare-package.mjs instead.
